From: Banyel3 <138186128+Banyel3@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 23:21:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(auditor): detect ledger reordering via ledger_digest

Wire ledger::ledger_digest into audit-stream as the ledger.order check.
When a run folder holds the chain read-back (ledger/ballots.ndjson, the
campaign ledger dump), the auditor now requires that the read-back is in
the chain canonical order (ascending nullifier, the order the chaincode
nullifier index serves it in) and that its ledger_digest equals the
ledger_digest of the served record put into that order. A permuted,
duplicated, dropped or altered read-back fails the audit; a folder with
no ledger dump gets no ledger.order finding, so offline runs and the
in-memory audit are unchanged.

ledger_digest now chains per-ballot leaves (v2 domain tags) so the
served side can be sorted without holding whole ballots. StreamAudit
gains an optional ledger_order field carrying the verdict and digest.
No wire, chaincode or campaign change.

